    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30540" root="عمر" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَمِرٌ</span></b>  <i>Visiting; a visiter.</i> (S, K.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <i>Performing the religious visit called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمْرَة</span>: (Kr, S:) <i>having
entered upon the state of</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِحْرَام</span> <i>for the performance
of that visit:</i> (TA:) pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَمِرُونَ</span>: and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُمَّارٌ</span> [a
pl. of ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَامِرٌ</span></b> ] is syn. with <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُعْتَمِرُونَ</span>. (Kr.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b3- 
And <i>Betaking himself to a thing; aiming at it;</i>

<i>purposing it.</i> (K, TA.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>Having his
head attired with an</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَمَارَة</span>, i. e. <i>a turban</i> [<i>&amp;c.</i>].
(AO, S.)

